{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And I will pass through.</b> To clear a path for My wrath (Psalms 78:50), so that no intermediary can act in this matter." "<b>And I will strike every firstborn.</b> For I distinguish between the drop of seed of a firstborn and the drop of seed that is not of a firstborn (Bava Metzia, chapter איזהו נשך)." "<b>And against all the gods of Egypt I will execute judgments.</b> I will humble the celestial princes who govern them now, so that the punishment will be felt more intensely." "<b>I am YHWH.</b> None of this is fitting for any but YHWH alone, as it says: אֲנִי ה', אֲנִי הוּא וְלֹא אַחֵר (Deuteronomy 32:39). With this He gives the reason for all the foregoing: why it was necessary that the blessed El Himself do all these things, and not as He did with Sennacherib and others (II Kings 19:35)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:09.971781036Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}